  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-47066" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Southern Africa Migration Management (SAMM) Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The European Union Regional Indicative programme (11th EDF RIP) for Eastern Africa, Southern Africa and the Indian Ocean (2014-2020) includes among its objectives the facilitation of legal migration and the prevention of irregular migration. On that basis, this action focuses on South -South migration flows, in complementarity to other initiatives developed for the Horn of Afria, the Sahel and North Africa. The comprehensive approach proposed by its Action addresses the specific objectives outlined in the 11th EDF RIP, taking into account the development-security-migration nexus, and also identifying positive spill-over effects of migration on regional integration and regional economic development. Four United Nations agencies (ILO, IOM, UNODC and UNHCR) will implement the Action. The overall objective of the programme is to improve migration management in the Southern Africa and Indian Ocean Region. In response to the outbreak of COVID-19 pandemic, some elements of the programme have been repurposed to provide support to vulnerable migrants in Southern African Development Community (SADC), aligned to the IOM Regional COVID Appeal. Interventions have been conducted in the areas of: Cross border coordination, Risk communication and Community engagement, Enhancing preparedness for Points of Entry (POE) and Direct assistance to vulnerable migrants.</narrative>
  </description>
